 **Auto-launch watcher `depth_canon_autolaunch.sh` (v10, round 3d; A5).** Armed by the Planner once every gate is closed; it waits for a valid GO token (`depth_canon_GO.token`: `head` == `git rev-parse HEAD`, `manifest_sha256` == sha256 of `depth_canon_pins.sha256`; re-checked before every launch) and for 3 consecutive clean 60-s polls (**v14:** ≥ 12,288 MiB free on each of GPUs 0 and 1; compute processes on them are co-tenants under the pinned `GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY=shared` — logged once per pid-set change, never dirty — and dirty only under `idle`; an `nvidia-smi` failure, a malformed row or an unknown uuid counts as dirty), then runs `MODE=SMOKE EXPECT_HEAD=<head>` and, on rc 0, `MODE=FULL` with the same head. A SMOKE refused by the launcher's GPU gate (rc 7: the memory floor or an unclean `nvidia-smi` answer; occupancy only under `idle`) is retried (≤ 5×, counter reset); any other failure is terminal (`FAILED`, FULL never attempted). Phases (WAITING_TOKEN → WAITING_GPU → SMOKE_RUNNING → FULL_RUNNING → DONE | FAILED) are written atomically to `depth_canon_autolaunch_state.json`; log `depth_canon_<TS>_autolaunch.log`; single instance (flock); flac interpreter enforced; it contains no `kill`, writes nothing outside the experiment folder and never touches the NAS itself. It is outside the training closure and therefore NOT in the pin manifest. It invokes the launcher with literal `MB=32 ACC=1 DRY_RUN=0` and scrubs every harness-only variable (v11, Codex rA W5b); the interpreter check is the launcher's exact pinned path; the token is exactly four newline-terminated `key=value` lines and nothing else (every logical line counts, blank ones too: keys = lines = newlines = 4; v12, Codex rA2 NIT 5) with a full ISO-8601 `issued` (what `date -Iseconds` prints) and `token_ok` also requires the pinned paths, the pins file, the launcher, the pin generator and the audit gate to be clean (a dirty file → WAITING_TOKEN, never terminal); transient = the launcher's rc 7 only (no text matching); the outer tee is drained at exit. Detached with `setsid nohup`; the Planner arms a Monitor on the state file.
 
 ## 5. Evaluation protocol (cells)
 
 Common flags for every generative cell: `--cond-method vanilla --cond-autocast bf16 --cfg-scale 1.0 --steps 1 --record-per-scene --record-stream --expected-stream-count <split size> --dump-scored-waveforms /media/diskstation/yixunhu/FLAC/exp25_pred_waveforms` (the ROOT; cell dir `<ROOT>/<metrics stem>`, v9); batch 64; EMA (`weights_source: ema` recorded). `--frame-avg-angles` is NOT passed (inert under vanilla; record `null`). Evaluator pin = one commit for every cell of the campaign (recorded `source_sha`).
 
 | Block | Cells | Protocol flags (in addition to the common set) | Count |
 |---|---|---|---|
 | **T** table | CANON@40k × K{1,8} × seeds 42–46 | `--canonicalize --rotate-mode fixed --rotate-deg 0` | 10 |
 | **T-dup** repeatability floor | CANON@40k × K{1,8} × seed 42 (re-run) | as T, `--eval-name …_dup` | 2 |
 | **C4+45** | CANON@40k × K{1,8} × θ{90,180,270,45} × seed 42 | `--canonicalize --rotate-mode fixed --rotate-deg <θ>` | 8 |
 | **R** random yaw | CANON@40k × K{1,8} × seeds 42–46 | `--canonicalize --rotate-mode random --rotate-seed <seed>` | 10 |
 | **D-i** mismatch diag | CANON@40k × K{1,8} × seed 42, θ=0 | `--allow-canon-mismatch` (no `--canonicalize`) | 2 |
 | **D-ii** P1 + canon diag | P1@40k × K{1,8} × seed 42, θ=0 | `--canonicalize --allow-canon-mismatch` | 2 |
 | **S** seen split (D5a) | CANON@40k × K{1,8} × seeds 42–46, `acousticroom_seeneval{_1,}.json` (`--expected-stream-count` = seen size) | `--canonicalize --rotate-deg 0` | 10 |
 | **P1-pin** one-pin comparator (D5b) | P1@40k × K{1,8} × seeds 42–46: T (θ=0) + R (random) + C4/45 (seed 42) | no `--canonicalize` | 10 + 10 + 8 |
 | **YAW-pin** one-pin comparator (A1) | YAW@40k, same cells as P1-pin, plus S (seen, 10) | no `--canonicalize` | 10 + 10 + 8 + 10 |
 | **TRAJ** (D5c) | CANON ckpts 2.5k…40k (16) × θ{0,90,180,270} × K{1,8}, seed 42 (the 40k θ cells are the T/C4 cells) | `--canonicalize --rotate-deg <θ>` | 120 new |
 | **ε_cond** probe | `depth_canon_cond_probe.py`, 64 unseen items × 5 offsets, fp32, GPU | — | 1 script |
 
 Totals: **230** generative cells (110 endpoint/diagnostic + 120 new TRAJ; review r2 nit) ≈ 230 × ~12 min / 2 GPUs ≈ 23 h (TRAJ ≈ 12 h of that, lowest priority, after the endpoint blocks); waveform dumps ≈ 230 × 260 MB ≈ 60 GB on the NAS (*sub-decision A3*).
 
 **Atomic cell completion (review r2 H3).** A cell now produces several required artifacts (metrics JSON, `.stream.json`, `.canon.json` when canonicalized, the waveform `.npy`, its `.sha256`, the manifest). `eval_FLAC.py` builds the waveform dump in a **same-filesystem staging directory** (`<final>.staging-<pid>`), verifies every artifact and checksum there, writes the `COMPLETE` marker **inside the staging directory last**, and only then atomically renames the already-complete directory to its final path (review r3 H2: a crash after the rename can no longer strand an unmarked, non-empty final directory). The driver's resume skips a cell **only** when the final directory carries the marker and the collector's verification of that cell passes; every final directory that fails the complete-and-verified predicate — unmarked, **or marker-bearing but collector-invalid** — and every leftover staging directory is quarantined (`<name>.incomplete-<ts>`) and reported before the cell is re-run. Tests simulate a crash immediately before and immediately after the rename. Dump directory names are derived from the metrics stem, so the filename injectivity test (§6 test 16) covers them too. **B-F** is NOT re-evaluated (fa eval ≈ 4×): it contributes its historical θ=0 row plus method-level A-F evidence only (no B-F@40k rotated cells exist) — the ledger below names every reused cell.
 
 **Comparator ledger** (review H5; written as `depth_canon_comparator_ledger.md` before the first result is quoted): for each reused cell — checkpoint path + sha, evaluator commit, protocol flags, seeds, aggregation, raw file path (or "md-quoted only" for exp_17's lost raws, which §5 replaces with YAW-pin). Random-yaw comparisons are CANON/P1/YAW at one pin; cross-recipe exp_14/15 random-yaw results are context only.
 
 Drivers: `depth_canon_eval_run.sh` (adapted from exp_17's extras runner: shared lock, two GPUs round-robin, skip-if-exists resume, per-cell logs, completion count, cell classes as data) and `depth_canon_collect.py` (reads raw JSONs + `.stream.json` + `.canon.json` + waveform manifests; verifies every record's protocol fields against its cell class **including the B2 binding fields**; pairs cells by (K, seed) and asserts identical `input_hash`; Tier 1 hash equality; Tier 2 waveform statistics from the dumps; Tier 3 aggregates (item-weighted AND per-scene), `Δ_C4`, seed-paired `Δ_R`; writes `depth_canon_results.md`). A `gen_model_comparison.py` row spec for CANON, P1-pin and YAW-pin (announcement 04) lands with the first T results; the four-arm matched-A6000 table in `_results.md` uses only one-pin rows plus B-F's historical row, labelled as such (review H6).
 
 **v10 (round 3c as built).** Cells are data: `depth_canon_cells.json` (230 rows = T 10, T-dup 2, C4+45 8, R 10, D-i 2, D-ii 2, S 10, P1-pin 28, YAW-pin 38, TRAJ 120; generated by `depth_canon_make_cells.py`, names injective through `build_output_paths`; `--blocks` selects the required set so A1 is a switch, `--no-dump-blocks` implements A3; flags written out explicitly incl. `--batch-size 64 --device cuda` and `--rotate-mode fixed --rotate-deg θ` on every fixed cell; YAW-pin uses `exp_15_yaw_aug_claude/FLAC_AR_YAWAUG.json`, byte-equal to the YAW checkpoint's embedded config). `depth_canon_eval_run.sh`: gates (lock, flac interpreter, **strict HEAD pin** `EXPECT_HEAD` = the campaign's one evaluator pin — kept strict by Planner decision: no commits on the branch during the ≈ 23 h campaign, records go to the FLAC checkout; committed-tree check; config pins; dump ROOT on the NAS share), checkpoints sha256-verified once per path against the NAS manifest and linked into a local farm `outputs_FLAC/exp25_depth_canon/<ARM>/` so metrics never land in `ar_40k_endpoints/`; two GPU lanes; the complete-and-verified resume predicate (marker + `depth_canon_collect.verify_cell`, which reads each dump once), quarantine of anything else, a required per-cell receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (checkpoint sha checked before the run, configs, argv, pin, lane, rc), TRAJ last. **Eval GPU policy (A6, landed in rB-F1):** a lane is used only when its card has ≥ 10 GiB free AND no foreign compute process (uuid-mapped, fail-closed queries, re-checked right before each spawn); `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (explicit opt-in by Yixun) relaxes the occupancy part only — **exercised for the whole exp_25 campaign by Yixun's 2026-10-25 shared-launch instruction (v14).** **v11 driver integrity (Codex rB B3/B4):** the relevant-tree content digest is taken at start, before every spawn and after every cell — any change is PIN DRIFT, exit 4, no further spawns, running cells finish; checkpoints are copied into a content-addressed verified cache `<farm>/.ckpt_cache/<sha>.ckpt` (hash while copying, 0444, atomic rename, free-space gate ≈ 14 GB) and hard-linked into the farm (an existing cache entry must satisfy the immutable contract — regular file, mode 0444, the source's size — and is fully re-hashed at staging AND immediately before EACH spawn; the post-run MEASURED sha256 goes into the receipt; r3c-style symlink farms are refused). **v12 (Codex rB2 B4):** `eval_FLAC.py` reads the checkpoint ONCE into memory, hashes that buffer and deserializes that same buffer (`torch.load(io.BytesIO(buf), map_location='cpu')`, arguments otherwise unchanged), recording `ckpt_sha256_loaded` + `ckpt_bytes_loaded` in every metrics record right after the base keys (records built without it stay byte-identical); `build_receipt` refuses unless loaded == measured == manifest sha and the loaded length == the driver's post-run `stat` (`--ckpt-bytes`); `verify_cell` requires record == receipt for both fields; `--nas-retention-audit` refuses `--dump-check receipt` (rB2 NIT). **Receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (A7, landed):** written only after the post-run full verification; carries the campaign/spawn/post digests, the checkpoint shas (expected + measured + loaded, with the loaded length), `artifact_sha256` of the metrics / `.stream.json` / `.canon.json`, and `dump_evidence` (verified dump manifest sha256, n, shape, dtype, waveform sha256, marker); `verify_cell(dump_check='receipt')` and `gen_model_comparison.py` validate OFFLINE from the committed files; `depth_canon_collect.py --nas-retention-audit` checks the bulk dumps separately. `depth_canon_collect.py`: `verify_cell` (protocol + B2 binding fields per cell class, manifest-level dump check), pairs by (arm, K, seed, step) with the `input_hash` proof, Tier 1 per-position hash equality + recomputed `canonical_depth_hash`, Tier 2 from the dumps via `depth_canon_stats`, Tier 3 (`Δ_C4`, 45° probe, seed-paired `Δ_R` on input_hash-equal pairs only), the table block (mean ± sd, item-weighted and per-scene), TRAJ grid, tie counts per cell and per split, `--partial` labels every heading PARTIAL and lists the missing cells; writes `depth_canon_results.{md,json}`. **Tier-2 control mapping (registered):** 45° → d64, 90° → d128, 180° → d256, 270° → d384, random → random; the pooled control p99 is the reference; matched-offset AND pooled rules plus the 1e-2 cap are all applied (fail-closed reading of "control p99"). The collector accepts as the Tier-2 reference **only** a probe artifact marked `registered: true` (run without `--diagnostic`, sidecar-verified, bound to the CANON@40k checkpoint sha); diagnostic probes are refused (Codex r3b HIGH 4; probe exit codes 0 registered PASS / 1 verdict FAIL / 2 refused / 6 diagnostic); **v11 (Codex rB B5):** a dirty tree is a registered deviation; the collector's `PROBE_CONTRACT` checks the evaluator pin == campaign pin, exact registered arguments, config + split hashes, load protocol, stream census, and renders `eps_cond = v; registered threshold 1e-05: PASS/FAIL` (missing / non-finite ε → artifact invalid). **Pairing (v11, Codex rB NIT):** `context_ids` has exactly K entries per item; strict uniqueness is NOT required because `AR_md` draws with replacement when a room has fewer than K other sources (520 of 6,337 unseen K = 8 targets; identical across the 11 exp_15 streams checked) — the registered rule is that every cell of one (split, K) repeats on the same targets; identical generative noise follows from the execution protocol (same arm/K/step/seed, batch size, census under the pinned evaluator), not from the hash preimage. The shared-map overlap count is derived from the validated audit and compared with the registered 1,093 items / 112 maps. `gen_model_comparison.py` gains the `exp25` contract (rows CANON / P1-pin / YAW-pin at the exp_25 pin, YAW-pin labelled re-measured; validation through `verify_cell`; a round = two-K pair at one pin); additive only.
 
 **Seen/unseen overlap disclosure (v10, Codex r3b data finding).** `acousticroom_seeneval.json` and `acousticroom_unseeneval.json` share **1,093 exact item paths (≈ 17–18 % of each) and 112 depth maps**. S-block rows are therefore correlated with T-block rows and are never presented as an independent replication; the collector prints the overlap count beside every seen-split table.
 
 ## 6. Tests (TDD, per function; `src/tests/`)
 
 Fixtures (review H8): deterministic synthetic depth tensors (`torch.Generator` seeded) passed through the **real** `convert_equirect_to_camera_coord`, with planted ties (same-column, cross-column on one row at separations {1, 64, 256}, exactly periodic images with period 256 and 128); no dataset-dependent test is load-bearing (one optional real-map test is marked `skipif` and duplicates a synthetic one).
 
 `test_depth_canon.py` (operator):
 1. `recover_depth_proxy`: equals the synthetic scalar depth to 1e-14 on the real converter's output; bitwise invariant (`torch.equal`) under `rotate_scene_metadata` for offsets {1, 64, 128, 300, 511}; rejects shape ≠ `[3,H,W]`, odd H, non-finite, integer dtype.
 2. `column_profile`: `[W]`, equals `D.max(0)`.
 3. `canonical_column` tie classes: unique → column, class `none`; several max pixels in one column → `same_column`; cross-column with distinct rooted images → `cross_column_image`; exactly periodic image (period W/2, W/4) → `StabilizedTieError` **regardless of the poses** (cases: distinct source azimuths, degenerate source, source exactly at a candidate column centre, context radii at `1e-6 − ulp` and `1e-6 + ulp`).
 4. **Exhaustive equivariance:** for every non-periodic fixture and **all 512 rolls**, `canonical_column(roll_d(md)) == (canonical_column(md) + d) mod W` and identical `tie_class`, with poses placed at `±π − ε`, `±π` (signed zero), `0`, exactly at column centres, and the degenerate source (poses must not influence the result). **Periodic fixture:** the operator raises `StabilizedTieError` for all 512 rolls, and the error's candidate set co-rotates.
 4b. Input contract: every one of the four pose fields is **required** (one missing-key test per field); `context_poses` and `context_poses_vit` share `N ≥ 1`; `canonicalize_scene_metadata` takes no `pose_keys` argument (all of `POSE_KEYS` are always rotated — a partial rotation would silently desynchronise the frame).
 5. `canonical_shift`: `(W − j*) mod W`; 0 iff `j* == 0`.
 6. `canonicalize_scene_metadata`: returns `(md', dj, tie_class)`; equals `rotate_scene_metadata(md, dj·2π/W, W)` field by field (`torch.equal`); post-condition `j* == 0`; idempotent; input not mutated; dtype/device preserved; `context_audio`/`scene`/`padding_mask` pass through by identity; exact pose-shape contract enforced (`[3]`, `[1,3]`, `[N,3]`, `[N,3]`, finite, floating).
 7. Invariance: `canonicalize(rotate(md, d))` vs `canonicalize(md)` — recovered-depth image `torch.equal`, vectors/poses `allclose(rtol=1e-5, atol=1e-6)`, d ∈ {1, 64, 128, 255, 256, 384, 511}, on fixtures with planted cross-column ties.
 8. Option-A negative control: the first-index rule fails test 4 on a planted tie (`xfail(strict=True)`).
 9. Raw-vs-proxy agreement: on the synthetic fixtures the candidate set and selected column from the scalar depth equal those from the proxy.
 
 `test_depth_canon_training.py` (wrapper + factory; tiny CPU `diffusion_cond` via the real factories as in `test_cond_dispatch.py`):
 10. `_parse_canonicalize_config`: absent → `{}`; `enabled:false` → `{}`; `enabled:"true"` → ValueError; unknown key → ValueError; missing/bool/negative `img_w` → ValueError; with `yaw_aug.enabled` → ValueError; with `cond_method fa_invariant` → ValueError; valid → exact kwargs.
