worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:105:**Auto-launch watcher `depth_canon_autolaunch.sh` (v10, round 3d; A5).** Armed by the Planner once every gate is closed; it waits for a valid GO token (`depth_canon_GO.token`: `head` == `git rev-parse HEAD`, `manifest_sha256` == sha256 of `depth_canon_pins.sha256`; re-checked before every launch) and for 3 consecutive clean 60-s polls (**v14:** ≥ 12,288 MiB free on each of GPUs 0 and 1; compute processes on them are co-tenants under the pinned `GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY=shared` — logged once per pid-set change, never dirty — and dirty only under `idle`; an `nvidia-smi` failure, a malformed row or an unknown uuid counts as dirty), then runs `MODE=SMOKE EXPECT_HEAD=<head>` and, on rc 0, `MODE=FULL` with the same head. A SMOKE refused by the launcher's GPU gate (rc 7: the memory floor or an unclean `nvidia-smi` answer; occupancy only under `idle`) is retried (≤ 5×, counter reset); any other failure is terminal (`FAILED`, FULL never attempted). Phases (WAITING_TOKEN → WAITING_GPU → SMOKE_RUNNING → FULL_RUNNING → DONE | FAILED) are written atomically to `depth_canon_autolaunch_state.json`; log `depth_canon_<TS>_autolaunch.log`; single instance (flock); flac interpreter enforced; it contains no `kill`, writes nothing outside the experiment folder and never touches the NAS itself. It is outside the training closure and therefore NOT in the pin manifest. It invokes the launcher with literal `MB=32 ACC=1 DRY_RUN=0` and scrubs every harness-only variable (v11, Codex rA W5b); the interpreter check is the launcher's exact pinned path; the token is exactly four newline-terminated `key=value` lines and nothing else (every logical line counts, blank ones too: keys = lines = newlines = 4; v12, Codex rA2 NIT 5) with a full ISO-8601 `issued` (what `date -Iseconds` prints) and `token_ok` also requires the pinned paths, the pins file, the launcher, the pin generator and the audit gate to be clean (a dirty file → WAITING_TOKEN, never terminal); transient = the launcher's rc 7 only (no text matching); the outer tee is drained at exit. Detached with `setsid nohup`; the Planner arms a Monitor on the state file.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:135:**Seen/unseen overlap disclosure (v10, Codex r3b data finding).** `acousticroom_seeneval.json` and `acousticroom_unseeneval.json` share **1,093 exact item paths (≈ 17–18 % of each) and 112 depth maps**. S-block rows are therefore correlated with T-block rows and are never presented as an independent replication; the collector prints the overlap count beside every seen-split table.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:173:`test_depth_canon_tie_audit.py` (23, v10): survivor detection = the operator's fail-closed branch; AR_md-built cloud vs raw-file selector; dedupe by resolved path; `--limit` forbids PASS (rc 4); dtype/shape contract violations are row errors (rc 3), never PASS; exit precedence INCOMPLETE (3) > FAIL (1) > REFUSED_SUBSET (4) > PASS (0); determinism across worker counts. `test_depth_canon_cond_probe.py` (24): stage chain pinned to `evaluate_model`'s key-strip / EMA selection / sampler; `--diagnostic` vs `registered` tagging; ARE refusal. ``test_depth_canon_collect.py` / `test_depth_canon_eval_run.py` / `test_gen_model_comparison_depth_canon.py` (+ `test_gen_model_comparison_data_curve.py` extended)` (25): cells manifest, driver (lanes, lock, resume predicate, quarantine, TRAJ last), collector (verify_cell, pairs, Tiers 1–3, control mapping, registered-probe refusals, partial mode, overlap disclosure), generator `exp25` contract. `test_depth_canon_autolaunch.py` (26, round 3d; subprocess-driven with a fake `nvidia-smi` and a fake launcher under a /tmp harness): no/stale/mismatched token → WAITING_TOKEN and no launch; busy GPUs → WAITING_GPU with the foreign process logged; counter reset on a dirty poll; three clean polls → SMOKE then FULL with the right env → DONE; GPU-gate failure → retry path, then FAILED after 5; any other SMOKE failure → FAILED without FULL; FULL failure → FAILED(rc); `nvidia-smi` failure = dirty; a commit between arming and firing → refusal; second instance → exit 2; launcher override without harness → exit 2; non-flac interpreter → exit 2; atomic, valid state JSON after every phase.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:188:9. **Recovery (v13; Yixun A8 + integrative review HIGH 2):** the launcher has NO gated resume MODE (P1 recipe: no `--ckpt-path`; FULL requires an empty namespace; the checkpoint-set gate assumes one launch marker), so an ad-hoc autonomous resume is NOT performed. If FULL crashes: prove no rank or launcher remains; preserve the namespace + logs; identify the latest complete 2,500-step boundary (bytes, sha256, length, step, parent launch marker, parent manifest); then resume ONLY through a reviewed path — preferably a `MODE=RESUME` launcher extension (TDD + guard cases + Codex review; built after FULL has launched, since the branch is frozen until then) or, if the crash precedes it, the six-step manual prescription kept in the FLAC-checkout HANDOFF (every pre-launch gate re-run by hand incl. the audit re-hash, NAS, W&B, DINO/init and strict two-GPU occupancy right before launch; the exact recipe with ONLY `--ckpt-path <verified boundary>` added, 40k endpoint / cadence / offline kept, a resume marker, a fresh W&B run id with the parent recorded; the same banner / both-rank / finite-loss / endpoint / tie-count / latency / checkpoint-ownership / exact-byte checks with tie + latency totals aggregated across legs; ONE explicit CANON lineage manifest — original hashes through boundary N, resumed hashes after N, no duplicate or foreign step, endpoint included — passed explicitly to the collector; full disclosure of crash, boundary, parent/child identities and the RNG/dataloader discontinuity). A resumed CANON arm remains a historical matched-recipe comparison (P1 itself resumed at 32.5k) but not a bit-identical trajectory pair.
