    27	- **Invariance of CANON, three tiers (review B3):**
    28	  - **Tier 1 — structural (exact):** for every item of a rotated cell (C4, 45°, random yaw) the sha256 of the *canonical recovered-depth image* equals the one of the same item in the θ=0 cell with the same seed and K: **6,337 / 6,337 equal**, by construction of §2.1 (the roll is integer arithmetic on a bitwise-stable proxy). Recorded in the `.canon.json` sidecar.
    29	  - **Tier 2 — practical waveform invariance (numerical; review r2 B2):** paired per-item relative L2 and L∞ between the scored waveforms of a rotated cell and its θ=0 pair (identical eval seed ⇒ identical generative noise and context draw, proven by identical `input_hash`). Denominators are pinned: `relL2 = ‖a−b‖₂ / max(‖b‖₂, 1e-6)`, `relL∞ = max|a−b| / max(max|b|, 1e-6)` with `b` the θ=0 waveform. Two controls bound the comparison: (i) the **determinism floor** — a duplicate θ=0 cell (same seed, run twice; expected exactly reproducible; it detects RNG/context/order drift only); (ii) the **numerical-composition control** (`depth_canon_cond_probe.py`, GPU, fixed noise): for 64 unseen items × offsets {64, 128, 256, 384, random}, direct `canon(md)` vs `canon(rot_d(md))` compared **stagewise** — conditioning tensors, the one-step velocity output, the sampled latent before decode, the decoded waveform — under the eval protocol (bf16 cond autocast, cfg 1.0, 1 step), mirroring exp_03's amplification diagnosis (conditioning 4.9e-8 → latent 3.7e-7 → waveform ~4.6e-4 fp32 / ~1.1e-3 autocast). **Pre-registered PASS rule:** the full-split rotated-vs-θ=0 distribution must satisfy `p99(relL2) ≤ 3 × p99` of the composition control's waveform relL2 (p99 = NumPy linear-interpolation percentile, as `depth_canon_stats.paired_summary` computes it; v9) **and** `p99(relL2) ≤ 1e-2` (hard cap); `max(relL2) ≤ 1e-1` is an **alarm bound** — not part of the PASS predicate, but exceeding it **suspends any unqualified invariance conclusion pending item-level triage** of the offending items (review r3); `relL∞` is reported descriptively (no threshold registered); the duplicate cell must be exactly reproducible (`max relL2 == 0`) as a separate determinism requirement. This is *practical* invariance — "round-off-level" is claimed only for Tier 1 and for the conditioning stage of the control (`≤ 1e-5`).
    30	  - **Tier 3 — metrics (secondary corroboration):** `Δ_C4(K)` = max−min over θ ∈ {0, 90, 180, 270}° (seed 42) and the 45° off-orbit probe; `Δ_R(K) = m_R − m_Z` seed-paired over seeds 42–46 (exp_14 random-yaw protocol). PASS if `Δ_C4` of CANON ≤ 10 % of P1's one-pin `Δ_C4` on every metric and `|Δ_R|` ≤ 1 eval-seed sd of `m_Z`.
    31	- `ε_cond` — **conditioning-level invariance (mechanism)**: the conditioning stage of the composition control above, additionally run in fp32 (autocast off): max relative L2 between the vanilla conditioning tensors of `canon(md)` and `canon(rot_d(md))`. Pre-registered PASS `≤ 1e-5` (expected ~1e-6; float32 rotation matrices). The analogue of exp_03's 4.9e-8.
    32	- **Comparator invariance (same pin, same box):** `Δ_C4` and `Δ_R` of **P1** and **YAW** re-measured at the exp_25 pin (§5), so the random-yaw comparison is a three-arm same-recipe comparison (CANON / P1 / YAW). **B-F** contributes its historical θ=0 quality row only, plus *method-level* FA invariance evidence from exp_08's fine-tuned A-F checkpoint (C₄ exact by construction; 45° structural residual) — there are no B-F@40k rotated cells on this box (ledger), and B-F is NOT part of the random-yaw comparison (review H5).
