worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_06-19-22_codex_code_rC4_review.log:3264:+**Planner:** Claude Fable 5.1 (main session, A6000 box `mae-cab-lab-server`) · **Date:** 2026-10-23 · **Status:** **v15** (2026-10-26 ≈ 06:00 EDT: projection cap under `shared` raised to 300 h after SMOKE 2 measured 19.27 s/step next to two 100 %-utilization co-tenants — 214 h, refused by v14's 120 h; everything else PASSED; v14.1 = 2026-10-26: prose sync of §4 watcher paragraph + §7 rung 5 to the v14 constants, Codex rC NIT; 2026-10-25: SHARED-GPU launch mode ordered by Yixun — memory-only GPU gate, floor 12 GiB, projection ≤ 120 h, co-tenants disclosed; W&B identity pre-check before the token; v13 = 2026-10-24 integrative pre-launch review **ARM**; arming scrub list; recovery policy = no ad-hoc resume; fix round rB-F3 for the probe; v12 = rB-F2 fix round as built after Codex re-verifications A2 + B2; v11 = rB-F1 after Codex reviews A + B; v10 = Codex r3b amendments, rounds 3c/3d, A5 = Yixun's pre-approved GO with unattended launch) — plan APPROVED at Codex plan r5 (v5); v8 adds the DDP-opaque metadata carrier found necessary by the round-2 code review (`depth_canon_codex_code_r2_review.md`, BLOCKING: PyTorch DDP's forward re-moves nested metadata tensors to CUDA after Lightning's transfer hook); **v6 amended §2.1 Step C after the round-1 CODE review**; v7 removes the stale v5 wording and adds the round-2 transfer-hook tests the code re-verification asked for (`depth_canon_codex_code_r1_reverify.md`: all code findings RESOLVED, operator ready) (`depth_canon_codex_code_r1_review.md`, BLOCKING: the pose-based keys C-2/C-3 are not exactly equivariant on float32 poses at column-centre / radius-threshold boundaries) — the tie-break is now the image key alone with fail-closed on any survivor, which is exactly equivariant and unreachable in registered runs under the rung-3 gate. Yixun's decisions D1–D6 recorded in §11. **Implementation: TDD round 1 (operator only, fully determined by D1) started under "build and review now"; rounds 2–3 and every launch wait for Yixun's confirmation of the v2 deltas A1–A3 (§11).**
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_06-19-22_codex_code_rC4_review.log:3297:+**Launcher `depth_canon_launch.sh`** — adapted from the reviewed exp_17 launcher with its r3 blocking findings applied AND the review-H9 gates: (1) reviewed-tree binding: pin **HEAD** and content-pin every file on the training path (`train.py`, `defaults.ini`, `src/data/*.py`, `src/models/*.py`, `src/training/*.py`, `src/inference/*.py`, `AR_md.py`, dataset config, split, VAE, control + arm config, the DINOv3 gate script) via a committed manifest; (2) smoke evidence must carry the same HEAD + manifest hash + `config contract OK`, and **a smoke is re-run after any review-driven source change**; (3) no `pipefail` around `tr | grep` — the log is read once into a variable after `wait`-draining the `tee` FIFO; (4) NaN/Inf check in FULL mode too; (5) **run-owned checkpoints**: FULL refuses a non-empty run namespace, every accepted checkpoint must be newer than the launch epoch, the cadence set must be exactly {2500, …, 40000}, foreign/stale files abort; (6) **NAS gate on the save filesystem**: mount identity (`findmnt`/`df` of the save path shows the CIFS share), a write-probe file, free space ≥ 30 GiB; (7) pinned smoke-projection threshold ≤ 60 h (**v14:** ≤ 120 h, because a shared card roughly halves the uncontended 0.259 opt-steps/s — the bound is a sanity cap on a co-tenant launch, not a speed target; **v15:** ≤ 300 h — SMOKE 2 (2026-10-26 05:38 EDT, `d838c8e`) measured the real contended rate next to two 100 %-utilization xRIR trainings: 19.27 s/step, ≈ 5× the uncontended 3.86 s/step, projected 214.1 h, so v14's 2× assumption was wrong by 2.5×; under `shared` the projection measures the co-tenants' load at that moment, which relaxes as they finish (their checkpoint cadence put GPU 0 free ≈ Oct 26 midday and GPU 1 ≈ Oct 27 05:00 EDT), so the cap keeps only its sanity role — 300 h ≈ 7× the uncontended 43 h still catches an order-of-magnitude pathology; the contended rate is disclosed in the evidence and the result tables as speed-only); **v10 (Codex r3b):** (8) GPU gate = ≥ 22.5 GiB free on BOTH cards **and zero foreign compute processes** on GPUs 0/1 (`nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps`; HIGH 7) — the launcher kills nothing; **v11:** every nvidia-smi query is strict (exit status checked apart from stdout, exactly one numeric memory row per card, malformed or unknown-uuid rows refuse) and every GPU-gate refusal exits with the DEDICATED **rc 7** (the watcher's only transient signal); **v12 (Codex rA2 HIGH 1/2):** rc 7 is emitted by ONE function (`gpu_refuse`) and an EXIT trap remaps any other exit 7 — `train.py`'s own status included — to the terminal **rc 8**, so a trainer failure is never retried; after the gate the co-tenancy disclosure issues NO further nvidia-smi query (it prints the strict gate's validated answers: free MiB + uuid per card, compute processes on other cards). **v14 (SHARED-GPU launch mode, ordered by Yixun 2026-10-25 ≈ 22:40 EDT — verbatim "please launch exp_25 if we have enough GPU free usage", then the AskUserQuestion choice "Relax the gates and launch shared now"):** the gate is MEMORY-ONLY: pinned `MIN_GPU_FREE_MIB=12288` (12 GiB per card; measured need of the identical `--batch-size 32 --num-gpus 2` recipe on this box: 5.9–6.6 GiB per rank in exp_14's smoke, ≈ 10.3 GiB per card for the exp_13 vanilla-B arm; the old 22.5 GiB floor was a margin, never a measurement), pinned `GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY=shared` (the other value, `idle`, restores the v10 refusal), the strict nvidia-smi parsing of v11 kept in full; foreign compute processes on GPU 0/1 are DISCLOSED (pid, card, used MiB, cwd) in the launch log and in the SMOKE evidence (`gpu_policy`, `min_gpu_free_mib`, `free_mib_at_launch`, `co_tenants_at_launch`) instead of refused; rc 7 stays reserved for the memory floor and unclean queries. Consequences carried as result disclosures: the FULL run and the campaign execute next to Yixun's xRIR exp_13/exp_28 chains (32 GiB each, 100 % utilization) and user dzheng's lanes — speed only, never the numbers; OOM risk in both directions (a co-tenant growing past the free memory kills whichever process allocates last; this launcher still never signals anything); the watcher's poll predicate mirrors the policy (foreign processes logged, memory floor decides). The eval campaign runs its lanes with `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (A6 opt-in, exercised by this instruction). Launcher exit codes: 0 ok · 2 a gate refused · 3 banner missing · 4 non-finite / SMOKE verdict FAILED · 5 checkpoint set wrong · 6 endpoint or two-rank start missing · 7 GPU gate (transient) · 8 a remapped 7 · anything else = `train.py`'s own status; (9) the interpreter is **enforced** (`command -v python` must resolve under `envs/flac/bin`; HIGH 6); (10) **tie-audit gate (BLOCKING 1; v11 = Codex rA A1 + rB B1):** SMOKE and FULL both refuse unless the committed, PINNED rung-3 audit report `depth_canon_tie_audit.json` + `.sha256` (in the pin set, committed at HEAD) passes THE one predicate `depth_canon_audit_gate.py` (`validate_tie_audit(audit_path, repo_root) -> (ok, problems, summary)`; CLI 0/1/2): sidecar, type-strict schema, `verdict PASS`, zero survivors/errors, full non-`--limit` coverage of the three splits, registered item counts, `dirty_code == ""`, no harness tag in production, the expected 9,650 unique map paths derived from the split JSONs through the audit script's own enumeration (path-set equality, no duplicates, typed rows), per-split census consistent with the rows, content hashes of the audit script / operator / `dataset.py` / `AR_md.py` / dataset configs / split JSONs, and a **re-hash of every current depth map** against the row hashes (8 threads inside a KILLABLE child process — the gate itself in `--rehash-worker` mode, own session — under the registered **900 s** wall-clock deadline `REHASH_DEADLINE_S`, no CLI or env override; read-only NAS, ≈ 2 min 15 s per launch; a timeout SIGKILLs the child's pr