worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:3:**Planner:** Claude Fable 5.1 (main session, A6000 box `mae-cab-lab-server`) · **Date:** 2026-10-23 · **Status:** **v15** (2026-10-26 ≈ 06:00 EDT: projection cap under `shared` raised to 300 h after SMOKE 2 measured 19.27 s/step next to two 100 %-utilization co-tenants — 214 h, refused by v14's 120 h; everything else PASSED; v14.1 = 2026-10-26: prose sync of §4 watcher paragraph + §7 rung 5 to the v14 constants, Codex rC NIT; 2026-10-25: SHARED-GPU launch mode ordered by Yixun — memory-only GPU gate, floor 12 GiB, projection ≤ 120 h, co-tenants disclosed; W&B identity pre-check before the token; v13 = 2026-10-24 integrative pre-launch review **ARM**; arming scrub list; recovery policy = no ad-hoc resume; fix round rB-F3 for the probe; v12 = rB-F2 fix round as built after Codex re-verifications A2 + B2; v11 = rB-F1 after Codex reviews A + B; v10 = Codex r3b amendments, rounds 3c/3d, A5 = Yixun's pre-approved GO with unattended launch) — plan APPROVED at Codex plan r5 (v5); v8 adds the DDP-opaque metadata carrier found necessary by the round-2 code review (`depth_canon_codex_code_r2_review.md`, BLOCKING: PyTorch DDP's forward re-moves nested metadata tensors to CUDA after Lightning's transfer hook); **v6 amended §2.1 Step C after the round-1 CODE review**; v7 removes the stale v5 wording and adds the round-2 transfer-hook tests the code re-verification asked for (`depth_canon_codex_code_r1_reverify.md`: all code findings RESOLVED, operator ready) (`depth_canon_codex_code_r1_review.md`, BLOCKING: the pose-based keys C-2/C-3 are not exactly equivariant on float32 poses at column-centre / radius-threshold boundaries) — the tie-break is now the image key alone with fail-closed on any survivor, which is exactly equivariant and unreachable in registered runs under the rung-3 gate. Yixun's decisions D1–D6 recorded in §11. **Implementation: TDD round 1 (operator only, fully determined by D1) started under "build and review now"; rounds 2–3 and every launch wait for Yixun's confirmation of the v2 deltas A1–A3 (§11).**
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:103:**Launcher `depth_canon_launch.sh`** — adapted from the reviewed exp_17 launcher with its r3 blocking findings applied AND the review-H9 gates: (1) reviewed-tree binding: pin **HEAD** and content-pin every file on the training path (`train.py`, `defaults.ini`, `src/data/*.py`, `src/models/*.py`, `src/training/*.py`, `src/inference/*.py`, `AR_md.py`, dataset config, split, VAE, control + arm config, the DINOv3 gate script) via a committed manifest; (2) smoke evidence must carry the same HEAD + manifest hash + `config contract OK`, and **a smoke is re-run after any review-driven source change**; (3) no `pipefail` around `tr | grep` — the log is read once into a variable after `wait`-draining the `tee` FIFO; (4) NaN/Inf check in FULL mode too; (5) **run-owned checkpoints**: FULL refuses a non-empty run namespace, every accepted checkpoint must be newer than the launch epoch, the cadence set must be exactly {2500, …, 40000}, foreign/stale files abort; (6) **NAS gate on the save filesystem**: mount identity (`findmnt`/`df` of the save path shows the CIFS share), a write-probe file, free space ≥ 30 GiB; (7) pinned smoke-projection threshold ≤ 60 h (**v14:** ≤ 120 h, because a shared card roughly halves the uncontended 0.259 opt-steps/s — the bound is a sanity cap on a co-tenant launch, not a speed target; **v15:** ≤ 300 h — SMOKE 2 (2026-10-26 05:38 EDT, `d838c8e`) measured the real contended rate next to two 100 %-utilization xRIR trainings: 19.27 s/step, ≈ 5× the uncontended 3.86 s/step, projected 214.1 h, so v14's 2× assumption was wrong by 2.5×; under `shared` the projection measures the co-tenants' load at that moment, which relaxes as they finish (their checkpoint cadence put GPU 0 free ≈ Oct 26 midday and GPU 1 ≈ Oct 27 05:00 EDT), so the cap keeps only its sanity role — 300 h ≈ 7× the uncontended 43 h still catches an order-of-magnitude pathology; the contended rate is disclosed in the evidenc